Integer coefficients for the element routines in this addon.


Base functions (shape functions)
--------------------------------

See file addons/README_basefunctions

Interpolations >=8 cannot yet be used for BCF.


Procedure pointers
------------------

Summary of assignment of user functions/subroutines to procedure pointers:

  coefficients%qinflow => qinflow    ! function for inflow boundary values of Q
  coefficients%brownian_vector => brownian_vector

NOTES:

 1) The user functions/subroutines only need to be assigned if they are
    actually being used. If a required assignment is forgotten an error message
    with be given.
 2) The user is free to choose the functions/subroutines for assignment as
    long as the interface is correct.


List of the coefficients
------------------------

  1-150: all relevant integer coefficients from the stokes & viscoelastic add-on
151-200: reserved for diffuse-interface add-on
201-250: reserved for inertia add-on
251-300: reserved for generalized Stokes add-on
301-350: reserved for compressible fluid add-on
351-400: reserved for deformation fields add-on
451-450: reserved for convection-diffusion-reaction using SUPG add-on

451: Q-vector tensor interpolation
    for a triangle
      2: P1
    for a quadrilateral
      4: Q1 

452: stochastic fluid model

453: start index in coefficient%r of the stochastic model material data
     The value must be at least 451.

454 log conformation transformation:
    0: no
    1: yes

455 Number of Q-fields

456 Time integration scheme for the Q-equation:
    1: explicit Euler
    2: backward Euler (implicit) for the force part 
    3: Crank-Nicolson (implicit) for the force part (only available for FENE)

457 numerical integration rule for boundary integrals in the DG method
    for curves:
      n: number of Gauss-Legendre integration points. 1<=n<=5. For example
         with n=3 a three-point Gauss-Legendre integration is used.
    for surfaces with quadrilaterals:
      n: number of Gauss-Legendre integration points in _one_ coordinate
         direction. 1<=n<=5. For example with n=3 a 3x3 Gauss integration is
         used for quads
    similar to coefficients%i(24) for macroscopic models using DG.

458-500 Reserved for future use. Set to zero for future compatibility.

